## Medical Leave

### Short-Term Disability

| Duration | Pay |
|----------|-----|
| Days 1-7 | 100% salary (sick leave) |
| Days 8-182 | 60% salary (STD insurance) |

**Eligibility**: All full-time employees, day 1

### Long-Term Disability

| Duration | Pay |
|----------|-----|
| After 182 days | 60% salary (LTD insurance) |

**Eligibility**: All full-time employees, day 1

### FMLA Leave

For eligible employees (12+ months, 1,250+ hours):

| Reason | Duration | Pay |
|--------|----------|-----|
| Own serious health condition | Up to 12 weeks | STD applies |
| Care for family member | Up to 12 weeks | Unpaid* |
| Military caregiver | Up to 26 weeks | Unpaid* |
| Qualifying exigency | Up to 12 weeks | Unpaid* |

*PTO may be used for pay during unpaid FMLA

### Medical Leave Process

1. Notify HR as soon as need is known
2. Complete FMLA paperwork (if applicable)
3. Provide healthcare provider certification
4. Coordinate with STD/LTD insurance
5. Check in with HR bi-weekly during leave
6. Return-to-work clearance from provider

